                        <summary>
                            
                            <p>This consists of three verses in Sanskrit and two in Tamil describing the fame and prowess of the Kēraḷa chief (or King) Adhikēndra Vyāmukhaśravaṇōjvala. His regal emblems of a parasol and a bow below it with what looking like <hi rend="italic">chāmara</hi> (flywisk) flanking either side of it are engraved below the inscription.</p>
                            
                        </summary>
